      "writtenOn": "2025-01-23T20:38:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sorry, the test run was on the child CL [here](https://android-review.git.corp.google.com/c/platform/art/+/3461585/2?checksPatchset\u003d1\u0026tab\u003dchecks). You\u0027ll see in the device boot logcats that there are several hiddenapi warnings (because it\u0027s only enabled in [warning mode](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:build/soong/scripts/gen_build_prop.py;l\u003d304;drc\u003d027601a8dab5a5d425f1b9ee2766c847c7983d52)). Several of those warnings are new with this CL, but there are cases when they\u0027re followed by crashes because the method got hidden for real, and that shouldn\u0027t happen.\n\nThe point with this CL is to be able to perform a check of hiddenapi access without regard to the policy, and so we get this caveat (which is why I added \"and the enforcement policy is applied\" above). `kCheckWithPolicy` has precisely the behaviour you\u0027re arguing for.\n\nApparently my comments aren\u0027t clear enough. I\u0027m open for suggestions how to make them better so the logic is explained adequately.",
